Additionally, stories featuring the same characters were printed through the 19 issues of ''Spider-Man Magazine'', published between March 1994 and March 1997, alongside stories inspired by the animated series ''[[Spider-Man (1994 TV series)|Spider-Man]]''.

====''X-Men '92''====
The comic book series ''[[X-Men '92]]'' was first released as one of the many tie-in titles for Marvel's 2015 ''[[Secret Wars (2015 comic book)|Secret Wars]]'' event, and continued in its second volume as a regular series in early 2016, starring characters of the TV show's reality.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.ign.com/articles/2015/03/13/x-men-the-animated-series-lives-on-in-x-men-92|title=X-Men: The Animated Series Lives On in X-Men '92|first=Jesse|last=Schedeen|date=13 March 2015|work=IGN|access-date=March 9, 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150330051428/https://www.ign.com/articles/2015/03/13/x-men-the-animated-series-lives-on-in-x-men-92|archive-date=March 30, 2015|url-status=live}}</ref>

In January 2022, Marvel announced a new series inspired by the cartoon, ''X-Men '92: House of XCII''. Published in April of that same year, the series explores an alternate universe where the events of [[Jonathan Hickman]]'s ''[[House of X and Powers of X]]'' happened decades earlier, in the '90s of the original show.<ref>{{cite web |last=Blum |first=Jeremy |date=14 January 2022 |title=X-Men: The Animated Series Meets House of X in New Marvel Series |url=https://www.cbr.com/x-men-92-house-of-xcii/ |access-date=21 January 2022 |website=[[Comic Book Resources|CBR]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240713002106/https://www.cbr.com/x-men-92-house-of-xcii/ |archive-date=July 13, 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

